namespace Lifestone.Client.Options;

public static partial class OptionCatalog
{
    /// <summary>
    /// The headless host's own options (M2 state track; parsed by src/Lifestone.Headless/HeadlessOptions.cs). The headless
    /// host also reads the Core options marked <see cref="OptionScenes.Headless"/> and the <see cref="Session"/> group.
    /// </summary>
    public static OptionGroup Headless() => new("Headless host", "dotnet Lifestone.Headless.dll",
    [
        new("--scenario", "login|holtburg-laps|academy-exit|mage-build|fighter-build|gear|buff|fight|death-and-regear|hunt|wayfind|journey|autopilot", "What the run does (default login: log in, enter the world, check the server mod's status, log off and quit). holtburg-laps walks laps around the Holtburg lifestone and academy-exit walks out of the Training Academy, both with zero server corrections required. mage-build finds or creates the test account's level-126 combat mage (the character name is fixed; --character and --create-character are ignored with a warning, and any --account but the default test account is refused), spends its experience and credits on the template, learns the arena profile's spells, then logs off; it is idempotent (a ready mage is only verified) and logs '[mage] verdict mage=<ready|built|failed> level=<n> template=<ok|short> spells=<n>/<m> built_steps=<n>'. fighter-build (M4 1.1) finds or creates the test account's level-40 fighter 'Holtburg Hunter' (the name is fixed; the same account rules as mage-build), spends its experience and credits on the fighter template, has the server mod grant its kit, wields the Mace, wears the five leather pieces, places it in Holtburg and logs off; idempotent (a ready fighter is only verified) and logs '[fighter] verdict fighter=<ready|built|failed> level=<n> template=<ok|short> kit=<ok|missing> wielded=<wcid|0> worn=<n>'. gear enters that mage (run mage-build first; the same character and account rules), has the server mod grant its kit (a wand, a leather set and the spell components of the arena profile, as the account casts them; a top-up), wields the wand and wears the five armour pieces, then logs off; it is idempotent (a ready mage sends no gear step: gear_steps counts the wand, the armour and the wields, topup counts the component requests, and the cast, when it is on, still burns components and mana) and logs '[gear] verdict gear=<wielded|failed> worn=<n> kit=<held>/<lines> gear_steps=<n> topup=<n> cast=<ok|fizzled|failed|n/a>' (cast is report-only: after the gear it enters the magic combat mode, casts one Creature Enchantment self buff, waits for the mana it needs and returns to non-combat). buff is the gear scenario without its cast, then the magic combat mode, the buff cycle of the profile's 24 lines (the --buff-* options; a regeneration wait is spent in non-combat), a forced re-buff pass that recasts the line closest to expiry while it is still active, non-combat and the log off (the same character and account rules; idempotent: a second run casts no self line) and logs '[buff] verdict gear=<wielded|failed> worn=<n> buffs=<active>/<wanted> levels=<line:level,..> rebuffed=<yes|no> forced=<yes|no> min_remaining_s=<s> transfers=<fired>/<tried> revitalizes=<n> fizzles=<n> mana_min=<n> cycle_s=<s> misses=<names|none>' (its default time limit is 3000 s). fight is the gear scenario, a buff top-up (the buff cycle runs only when a profile line is missing or has under 600 s left), the teleport to the Aluvian Black Spawn Den, the magic combat mode and a Flame Bolt fight against the Tusker Slaves of the arrival's floor until --fight-kills kills (default 1) or --fight-seconds (default 300), walking the floor when nothing is in range or three casts miss, then non-combat and the log off (the same character and account rules); it logs '[fight] verdict gear=<wielded|failed> worn=<n> buffs=<skipped|topped-up:<n>> kills=<n> damage_dealt=<n> spells_cast=<n> misses=<n> xp_gained=<n> damage_taken=<n> hits_taken=<n> evades=<n> level=<I-VII> range_m=<m> projectiles=<n> walks=<n> fight_s=<s>' (its default time limit is 3600 s). death-and-regear (M3 3.2) is the gear scenario, then the mage's spell bars (bar 1 the arena profile's lines, bar 2 Flame Bolt I to VII; only the spells a bar lacks are sent), a bind at Holtburg's lifestone (the Holtburg point of interest, the nearest lifestone object, a Use on it), the teleport to the Aluvian Black Spawn Den, a suicide there when any enchantment but the vitae is active (a death removes every enchantment, so the mage meets the tuskers unbuffed), a walk to the nearest tusker cell and non-combat among the Tusker Slaves until they kill the mage (--death-seconds, default 600), the respawn at the lifestone, the gear scenario again (what the death dropped is spawned again, the wand and the five pieces wielded) and the log off (the same character and account rules); it changes the character (vitae, dropped items, a corpse in the den) and logs 'death ok=<true|false> died=<n> suicides=<n> vitae=<pct> respawn=<lifestone|elsewhere|none> corpse=<n> purged=<n> protected=<n> vitals_pct=<x|n/a> gear_restored=<yes|no> worn=<n> hits_taken=<n> damage_taken=<n> evades=<n> health_min_pct=<x|n/a> death_s=<s|n/a> death_frame_max_ms=n/a fight_frame_max_ms=n/a deaths=<n> corpses_stale=<n> protection=<dispelled|expired|none> vitae_paid=<xp|n/a> vitae_after=<pct|n/a> bars=<set:n|ok|n/a> unbuff=<suicide|none|n/a> bound=<yes|no>' (its default time limit is 900 s plus --death-seconds). hunt (M4 1.2) enters the test account's level-40 fighter 'Holtburg Hunter' only (the same account rules as fighter-build), binds it at Holtburg's lifestone, uses a Potion of Healing (at most 2) when its health is under 60%, teleports it to the first dry cell of the Low B belt (the level 8 to 20 ground south-west of the town), picks the nearest creature of the belt's names and fights it with --hunt-weapon until --hunt-kills kills (default 1) or --hunt-seconds (default 300), then sets non-combat, restores the Mace, teleports back to Holtburg and logs off; a health fall under 30% cancels the attack and returns (the run fails with returned=yes); it logs 'hunt fighter=<ok|wrong> kills=<n> swings=<n> shots=<n> hits=<n> misses=<n> damage_dealt=<n> damage_taken=<n> hits_taken=<n> evades=<n> xp_gained=<n> returned=<yes|no>' (all report-only), and changes the character (experience, vitae, healing potions) its default time limit is 600 s plus --hunt-seconds. wayfind (P5a S6) logs in as the fighter of --account (test-melee: Holtburg Brawler, test-archer: Holtburg Archer, test: Holtburg Hunter), optionally places it at --from, runs to --to with the wayfinder and the human keys through the headless streamer, with --wayfind-back runs back, prints the wayfind lines (see --to) and logs off; its default time limit is the straight-line route at 4.8 m/s plus 300 s per leg. journey (M4 P5b) runs one of the three journeys of --journey (mage on test, melee on test-melee, archer on test-archer; without --account the journey's own account): one login, the plan's stations in order from Holtburg's lifestone (the scenario options --hunt-*, --fight-*, --death-*, --buff-*, --vitals-* and --heal-* apply to the stations), on foot through the wayfinder's runner over the headless streamer, the plan's teleport budget, and the log off; it prints one 'journey station=<name> ok=<true|false> s=<s> <fields>' line per station and 'journey done ok=<true|false> name=<plan> stations=<n>/<m> ...' at the end; its default time limit is the plan's expected seconds plus 300 s. autopilot (M5 item 4, D57) is BSD Mage's outer loop on the test account: one login, then the journey's own stations (the buff, the travel to the ground, an open-ended fight, the logistics trip, the death handler) in a loop by the autopilot's state machine until a stop rule (--autopilot-minutes, --autopilot-level) or a stop request ends it, then the log off; its options are the --autopilot-* ones and the stations' (--fight-*, --death-*, --buff-*, --vitals-*), --journey may only say mage, and the host's time limit is lifted for it (the stop rules end the run; with --autopilot-minutes a ceiling of that many minutes plus 1,500 s, with none no limit; --quit-after still sets one). It prints the bare lines 'autopilot cycle n=<n> state=<death|trip|stopped> kills= ...' per cycle and 'autopilot done ok=<yes|no> cycles=<n> stop=<why> ...' at the end; the exit code is 0 only when the done line says ok=yes."),
        new("--journey", "mage|melee|archer|hero-archer|hero-brawler|hero-mage|mage-corpses", "Which journey runs (mage-corpses: M5 7, the one-off clean-up of BSD Mage's den corpses): --scenario=journey (headless) or --login-check=journey (the main scene; M4 P5b; required by those two, refused by every other; the main scene runs it with `tools\\godot.ps1 -Run -Offscreen -IsolateUserData -TimeoutSeconds N -GameArgs:'--login-check=journey --journey=melee --account=test-melee'`, takes the plan's test account, and its station frames are <stem>-station-<name>.png with --play-screenshot=PATH): mage is BSD Mage on test (build check, gear, buff with the driver's pass, cast facts, the kit refusal, harm-heal, bind, the den, the den fight, one death, Lifestone Recall home), melee is Holtburg Brawler on test-melee (build check, buff, bind, the belt hunt, harm-heal, Lifestone Recall home, the vendor, the chests) and archer is Holtburg Archer on test-archer (build check, buff, bind, the forest hunt, appraisals, harm-heal, Lifestone Recall home, the vendor, the shortcuts). A different --account fails the run. The hero journeys (M4 P5b J7, never in the gate; the lead runs them alone with --journey-shots at the hero video's size) are hero-archer (Holtburg Archer on test-archer: build check, buff, bind, the forest hunt with Greater Frost Arrows, Lifestone Recall home), hero-brawler (Holtburg Brawler on test-melee: the belt hunt with the Mace) and hero-mage (BSD Mage on test: build check, which teaches Cassius' Ring of Fire (1785), gear, buff, bind, the den travel by Primary Portal Recall, the den fight casting the Ring of Fire at the tuskers, Lifestone Recall home).", AlsoIn: OptionScenes.Main),
        new("--fighter", "hunter|melee|archer", "Which fighter template --scenario=fighter-build builds and --scenario=hunt hunts with (M4 P4): hunter is Holtburg Hunter on account test (the Mace and the Shortbow), melee is Holtburg Brawler on test-melee (Heavy Weapons, the Mace, no bow) and archer is Holtburg Archer on test-archer (Missile Weapons, the Shortbow and 500 Arrows, no Mace). The default follows --account (test = hunter, test-melee = melee, test-archer = archer); a value that does not match --account fails the run."),
        new("--fighter-recreate", "on|off", "Opt-in for --scenario=fighter-build on test-melee or test-archer only (the Brawler and the Archer; refused for the Hunter, on any other account and for any other scenario; M4 P5a C5, owner decision D40): when the existing fighter was created with attribute values other than its template's (the build otherwise fails with template=mismatch:<attribute> <have>/<want> before it buys anything), the build logs off, deletes that character through the client's retail character delete (the character stays pending deletion, restorable in ACE's window; ACE frees the name at once), waits for the server to list it as pending deletion, creates the template's character through the normal creation and builds it to the target; it logs 'recreated=yes old=pending-deletion' in the verdict. With no mismatch it does nothing extra. It never uses the server mod's purge. Default off.", ValueOptional: true),
        new("--fresh-character", "on|off", "The live gate's re-create (M4 fresh-character item, owner decisions D44 and D45): for --scenario=fighter-build on test-melee or test-archer (the Brawler and the Archer) and for --scenario=mage-build on the default account test (the BSD Mage); refused for the Hunter, on any other account, for any other scenario and together with --fighter-recreate. The template's live character is never entered: it is deleted from the character list through the retail character delete (the character stays pending deletion), the build waits for the list to show it pending, creates the template's character and builds it as usual (with no live copy it only creates it); then the new copy purges the old copies of its own name with the server mod's char purge until the mod answers unknown-character (never another character; the mod needs the D45 rule: a pending row named like a build character may be purged while a live copy of that name is on the account), and is placed in Holtburg. The purge comes only after the build ended met, so a failed build leaves the old copy restorable. The build fails when a re-created character's old copy was not purged. The verdict gains 'fresh=recreated|created purged=<n>'. Default off.", ValueOptional: true),
        new("--mage-level", "L", "The level the BSD Mage build reaches, for --scenario=mage-build, and for --scenario=journey --journey=mage, whose build-verify station then judges the mage by that level's plan, M5 item 7 F14 (M5 item 7 F3, owner decision D87; default 126, the template's level; 50 to 126). The soak's mage is built at 80 (`--scenario=mage-build --fresh-character --mage-level=80`): it casts level VI from the ground's spell plan and has fewer ranks. The build sends the experience of that level (the XpTable's), creates and trains the mage and judges the character by that plan (the verdict's level= and template=). Below 126 the mage is the TRADITIONAL mage (M5 7 F6, owner decision D87 amended, a traditional mage soaks the damage): no Melee Defense at all (untrained), War Magic and Life Magic specialised at creation (28 + 20 of the heritage's 52 skill credits), Creature Enchantment, Item Enchantment and Mana Conversion trained afterwards (8 + 8 + 6 of the 4 spare and the levels' credits: all three from level 32, so every level this option takes trains them), the experience spent on the spending rule with the dance shares (more for Endurance and Max Stamina, which the stamina-to-mana dance feeds on) and Melee Defense's share rolled to the other stats. Level 126 is the gate's build as ever (War Magic and Melee Defense specialised, Life Magic trained). A skill the credits cannot pay for is left out and named in a loud line (TODO(m5-mage-level-credits)). A level below 50 (which cannot train Life Magic, Creature Enchantment and Mana Conversion), a value that is no number and another scenario are refused. The live gate re-creates the mage at 126 (its --fresh-character run takes no --mage-level)."),
        new("--gear-grant-only", "WCID:COUNT", "M5 7 D146, the owner's exception to DoD 6 for one test run: --scenario=gear grants exactly COUNT (1 to 100) of the one weenie WCID over the item verb, counts the pack before and after, and logs off; no kit top-up, no wield, no cast."),
        new("--laps", "N", "Laps of the Holtburg route for --scenario=holtburg-laps (default 3)."),
        new("--create-character", "NAME", "Use this character, creating it first on the account when it does not exist."),
        new("--summary", "PATH", "Also write the run's summary as JSON to PATH (relative to the repository root, never under src/ or tests/); it holds no secrets."),
    ], OptionScenes.Headless);
}
